From 360acd35a55d89f7ce3b29d885d079ed13c0a54c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jolyon Brown <jolyon@limilo.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:17:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 33/38] Keep the sum's destination when hoisting an add across
 a call

MoveCLCLoadAddZPStoreUp moves "CLC; LDA zp1; ADC zp2; STA zp3" up to where
its operands were last written.  It checked that the instructions it moves
past do not read zp3 (UsesZeroPage), but not that they do not write it: a
JSR to a callee that loads its stack parameter into the accumulator
registers overwrites a sum hoisted into $1b, and RemoveUnusedResultInstructions
then deletes the sum and its loads.  A char result built from two values
read before a call to an address-taken function came back as whatever the
callee left in $1b (nethack64 repro r45; upstream bf42402 exposes it, by
no longer taking such a callee's parameters as constants).  Check
ReferencesZeroPage, which covers both.

Found by Codex; checked by Claude.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp b/oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp
index 527f32d..08a31a7 100644
--- a/oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp
+++ b/oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp
@@ -44665,7 +44665,9 @@ bool NativeCodeBasicBlock::MoveCLCLoadAddZPStoreUp(int at)
 			return false;
 		if (mIns[j].ChangesZeroPage(mIns[at + 2].mAddress))
 			return false;
-		if (mIns[j].UsesZeroPage(mIns[at + 3].mAddress))
+		// The hoisted result must survive until the original store, including
+		// calls that clobber its destination without reading it.
+		if (mIns[j].ReferencesZeroPage(mIns[at + 3].mAddress))
 			return false;
 		if ((mIns[at + 2].mLive & LIVE_CPU_REG_C) && mIns[j].ChangesCarry())
 			return false;
